From 0eb0e3015ff032f74952d3b35fa5b4bf84fa2728 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Tada Antunes <leonardotada@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:30:36 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] docs: rename to steadygc, add the fork links and the clone
 URL

The project name in the documentation and in the labels printed by the bench
scripts changes from oneday to steadygc (81 lines, 16 files; the collector's
sources never used the old name). The collector's run-time option is unchanged:
it is still gc:sdc / gc:sdcq. README.md gets the clone URL, and guide/usage.md a
"Where the code is" section with the three repositories and the branches of the
DMD and LDC forks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012VbUx1Wv1w4QgcvdgLK8qz
